WEBVTT

cue-VID_U5_04-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Paw and Polish Grooming sells shampoos, brushes and grooming sessions. An Income Statement covers a period; a statement of financial position shows the value of assets and liabilities at a particular time. Picture a balance scale frozen on one date. On the left sit assets; on the right sit liabilities and equity. The scale must balance, because everything the business owns was funded by either creditors or owners.

cue-VID_U5_04-2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Load the left pan. Non-current assets are property, machinery and other assets not turned into cash within one year: grooming tables, dryers and the shop leasehold, worth one hundred eighty thousand dollars. Current assets become cash within one year: twenty-four thousand of inventory, sixteen thousand of trade receivables and ten thousand of cash. That is fifty thousand dollars of current assets. Total assets are one hundred eighty thousand plus fifty thousand, or two hundred thirty thousand dollars.

cue-VID_U5_04-3
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Fill the right pan. Current liabilities are short-term debts due within one year: thirty thousand dollars owed to suppliers and a ten-thousand-dollar overdraft, totalling forty thousand. Non-current liabilities are long-term debts repaid over more than one year: a seventy-thousand-dollar bank loan for equipment. Total liabilities are forty thousand plus seventy thousand, or one hundred ten thousand dollars. The right pan is still far lighter than the left, so the owners' equity is needed to balance the scale.

cue-VID_U5_04-4
00:01:32.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Equity completes the right pan. The owners invested one hundred twenty thousand dollars. Add current liabilities of forty thousand, non-current liabilities of seventy thousand, and equity of one hundred twenty thousand. Forty plus seventy plus one hundred twenty equals two hundred thirty thousand dollars. The scale levels perfectly: total assets of two hundred thirty thousand equal total liabilities plus equity. If the two sides did not agree, a figure would be missing.

cue-VID_U5_04-5
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Two derived figures matter. Working capital is current assets minus current liabilities: fifty thousand minus forty thousand equals ten thousand dollars. Capital employed, defined here as total assets minus current liabilities, is two hundred thirty thousand minus forty thousand, or one hundred ninety thousand dollars. Check it the other way: non-current assets of one hundred eighty thousand plus working capital of ten thousand also gives one hundred ninety thousand.

cue-VID_U5_04-6
00:02:34.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Assess liquidity. The Current Ratio is current assets divided by current liabilities: fifty thousand over forty thousand gives one point two five to one. The Acid-Test Ratio removes inventory: fifty thousand minus twenty-four thousand is twenty-six thousand, divided by forty thousand gives zero point six five to one. Because nearly half of current assets, forty-eight percent, are shampoos and brushes in stock, therefore the firm depends on selling inventory, so its liquid cover is weaker than the first ratio suggests.

cue-VID_U5_04-7
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:36.000
A statement of financial position is useful to lenders and owners, because it shows what is owed and what is owned. But it is a snapshot: figures are at historical cost, not today's market value; goodwill and staff skill are absent; and one date can hide a seasonal cash gap. A single list of balances cannot show profit earned during the year. Read it alongside the Income Statement before lending or investing.

cue-VID_U5_04-8
00:03:36.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Rebalance the scale one last time. Left pan: non-current assets one hundred eighty thousand, current assets fifty thousand, total two hundred thirty thousand. Right pan: current liabilities forty thousand, non-current liabilities seventy thousand, equity one hundred twenty thousand, total two hundred thirty thousand. Working capital ten thousand; capital employed one hundred ninety thousand. Current Ratio one point two five; Acid-Test Ratio zero point six five. The picture is clear at a glance, yet only for this one date.

